@startuml
title Database endpoints - shared request transaction and errors
hide footbox
actor Client
participant "FastAPI / Pydantic" as API
participant "get_db / transaction" as TX
database PostgreSQL as PG
Client -> API: Request
alt Invalid path, query, or body
  API --> Client: 422 {detail: ...}
else Valid input
  API -> TX: Request database session
  alt DATABASE_URL not configured
    TX --> API: HTTPException 503
    API --> Client: 503 {detail: ...}
  else Engine configured
    TX -> TX: Open session and transaction
    API -> TX: Execute route queries / mutations
    TX -> PG: SQL (flush may execute writes)
    alt Route raises HTTPException (404 / 409 / 422)
      TX -> PG: ROLLBACK
      TX --> API: Propagate HTTPException
      API --> Client: Original status {detail: ...}
    else IntegrityError (including commit failure)
      TX -> PG: ROLLBACK
      TX --> API: Sanitized HTTPException 409
      API --> Client: 409 {detail: ...}
    else OperationalError (including commit failure)
      TX -> PG: ROLLBACK
      TX --> API: Sanitized HTTPException 503
      API --> Client: 503 {detail: ...}
    else Route and serialization succeed
      TX --> API: Route result
      API -> API: Validate / serialize response
      API -> TX: Exit function-scoped dependency
      TX -> PG: COMMIT before sending success
      API --> Client: 200 / 201 / 204
    end
    TX -> TX: Close session
  end
end
note over API, PG
Only expected error mappings are shown.
Unexpected exceptions abort the transaction and propagate.
Health and framework documentation routes do not use get_db.
end note
@enduml
